<title>USA: TABLE - Guitar Center Inc Q2 results.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Guitar Center Inc Q2 results.</headline>
<dateline>AGOURA HILLS, Calif. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended	 Six months ended</p>
<p>				 Jun 30,  Jun 30,    Jun 30,  Jun 30,</p>
<p>				   1997	1996	 1997     1996</p>
<p>				(in thousands, except per-share data)</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>before deferred</p>
<p>  compensation expense   $ 5,430  $ 3,594    $10,103  $ 7,481</p>
<p>Pro forma interest</p>
<p>  expense (a)		  1,896    1,896	3,792    3,792</p>
<p>Pro forma income before</p>
<p>  income tax		   3,534    1,698	6,311    3,689</p>
<p>Pro forma income taxes (b)</p>
<p>				   1,343	645	2,398    1,402</p>
<p> Pro forma net income	2,191    1,053	3,911    2,287</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		 20,493   20,420     20,456   20,420</p>
<p>Adjusted pro forma net</p>
<p>  income per share	    0.11     0.05	 0.19     0.11</p>
<p>(a)  If the initial public offering, including the exercise of the underwriters' over-allotment option, and the resulting redemption of $33.3 million principal amount of long-term debt, had been consummated on Jan. 1, 1997, then the interest expense on the Senior Notes would have been reduced by $231,000 to $1,896,000, and $1,268,000 to $3,792,000 for the three and six months ended June 30, 1997, respectively.</p>
<p>(b)  Pro forma income taxes reflects an estimated statutory provision of 38 percent for income taxes.  As of Dec. 31, 1996 the company had net operating loss carry forward for federal income tax purposes aggregating $64.2 million, which has been fully reserved.</p>
